  "content": {
    "problemStatement": "There is a multiset SSS containing N+MN + MN+M strings, NNN of which are \"&lt;&lt;&lt;\" and MMM of which are \"&gt;&gt;&gt;\".\n\nFor two strings sss and ttt, f(s,t)f(s, t)f(s,t) is defined as:\n\n\n\nIf sss is smaller than ttt in lexicographical order, f(s,t)=s+f(s, t) = s +f(s,t)=s+ \"&lt;&lt;&lt;\" +t+ t+t;\n\n\n\n\nIf sss is equal to ttt in lexicographical order, f(s,t)=s+f(s, t) = s +f(s,t)=s+ \"===\" +t+ t+t;\n\n\n\n\nIf sss is larger than ttt in lexicographical order, f(s,t)=s+f(s, t) = s +f(s,t)=s+ \"&gt;&gt;&gt;\" +t+ t+t;\n\n\n\nYou need to perform N+M−1N + M - 1N+M−1 operations. Each time, choose two strings sss and ttt in SSS, insert f(s,t)f(s,t)f(s,t) to SSS and erase sss and ttt from SSS.\n\nFinally, only one string remains in SSS. Find the lexicographically smallest possible final string.\n\nIn lexicographical order, string are compared based on their characters from left to right, similar to how words are ordered in a dictionary. The comparison follows these rules:\n\n\nThe first character of each string is compared. The string with the smaller character (based on its ASCII value) is considered smaller.\nIf the first characters are the same, the second characters are compared, and so on, until a difference is found.\nIf one string is a prefix of the other, the shorter string is considered smaller.\nIn this context, the characters \"&lt;&lt;&lt;\", \"===\", and \"&gt;&gt;&gt;\" have the following lexicographical order:\n\n\n\"&lt;&lt;&lt;\" is the smallest (ASCII value 60),\n\"===\" is the second (ASCII value 61),\n\"&gt;&gt;&gt;\" is the largest (ASCII value 62).\n\nInput Format\n\nThe first line of input will contain a single integer TTT, denoting the number of test cases.\nEach test case consists of multiple lines of input.\n\nThe only line of each test case contains two space-separated integers NNN and MMM.\n\n\n\n\nOutput Format\nFor each test case, output the lexicographically smallest possible final string.",
    "constraints": [
      "1≤T≤1041 \\leq T \\leq 10^41≤T≤104",
      "0≤N,M≤2⋅1050 \\leq N,M \\leq 2 \\cdot 10^50≤N,M≤2⋅105",
      "N+M≥2N+M \\ge 2N+M≥2",
      "The sum of NNN and MMM over all test cases won't exceed 2⋅1052 \\cdot 10^52⋅105, respectively."
    ],
